! ============================================================
! Same topology, different deployment shape: a plain perimeter NGFW
! sitting at Level 3.5, NOT host-routed. Devices on VLANs 12-15 talk
! to each other directly over the L3 switch fabric; this appliance
! never sits in that path and therefore has no policy — and, more
! importantly for the compliance engine, no traffic evidence either —
! covering area-to-area (east-west) reachability. Its ACL only ever
! contains north-south rules. Used for case04 (evidence abstention).
! ============================================================

access-list OT-PERIMETER extended permit tcp 10.4.0.0 255.255.0.0 host 10.40.0.11 eq 443
access-list OT-PERIMETER extended permit tcp 10.4.0.0 255.255.0.0 host 10.40.0.12 eq 443
access-list OT-PERIMETER extended permit tcp 10.4.0.0 255.255.0.0 host 10.40.0.13 eq 443
access-list OT-PERIMETER extended deny ip 10.4.0.0 255.255.0.0 any log

access-list OT-PERIMETER extended permit tcp host 10.30.0.11 host 10.40.0.11 eq 1433
access-list OT-PERIMETER extended permit tcp host 10.40.0.12 host 10.30.0.10 eq 443
access-list OT-PERIMETER extended permit tcp host 10.40.0.12 host 10.30.0.11 eq 443
access-list OT-PERIMETER extended permit tcp host 10.40.0.12 host 10.30.0.12 eq 443
access-list OT-PERIMETER extended permit tcp host 10.40.0.13 host 10.30.0.12 eq 3389
access-list OT-PERIMETER extended deny ip 10.40.0.0 255.255.255.0 any log

! No entries below this line for VLAN 12/13/14/15 traffic — a plain
! perimeter box was never in that path and has nothing to say about it.
access-list OT-PERIMETER extended deny ip any any log
